  "worked_solution": "The graph shows that as we approach $h=0$ from the left, the $y$ value approaches $-10.$ So, the left-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{h\\to \\,{0}^{-}}g(h)=-10.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, when we approach $h=0$ from the right, the $y$ value approaches $-10.$ So, the right-hand limit is\n\n$$\n{lim}_{h\\to \\,{0}^{+}}g(h)=-10.\n$$\n\nSince both the left and right-hand limits exist and are equal to $-10,$ we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{h\\to \\,0}g(h)=-10.\n$$",
